WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.262
Three baselines close the module.

2
00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:05.021
The AD CS that remains keeps running for

3
00:00:05.021 --> 00:00:08.363
months or years for BRIDGE
and RETAIN workloads.

4
00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:11.671
Remove every template
those workloads don't need

5
00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:14.576
from each CA's issuance
list; it's reversible.

6
00:00:14.576 --> 00:00:18.513
Alert on requests for templates
that should no longer be requested.

7
00:00:18.513 --> 00:00:23.912
Keep CRL publication on schedule, and test
it from representative client networks.

8
00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:26.375
Back up the CA before every change.

9
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:30.120
Treat CA servers as Tier 0,
the program's designation,

10
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.475
because the CA can mint domain
authentication credentials.

11
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:40.059
And the program requires FIPS
140-2 or 140-3 validated modules,

12
00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:46.737
CA keys held non-exportable in an HSM,
and dual control for root ceremonies.

13
00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:51.375
Cloud PKI removes most of that
attack surface but adds its own.

14
00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:55.869
Scope administrators with custom
Intune roles and scope tags;

15
00:00:55.869 --> 00:00:59.412
there's no built-in Intune
PKI Administrator role.

16
00:00:59.412 --> 00:01:01.363
EKUs are fixed at creation.

17
00:01:01.363 --> 00:01:07.780
On Windows, set the key storage provider
to TPM, otherwise fail; a 4096-bit key

18
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:14.612
can only live in the software provider, so
the program uses 2048-bit RSA in the TPM.

19
00:01:14.612 --> 00:01:16.824
The program sets one-year validity.

20
00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:19.600
And don't build production
CAs during a trial.

21
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.225
Entra CBA is a relying party, so its
hardening is about trust and binding.

22
00:01:25.225 --> 00:01:28.075
Require high-affinity
bindings in production.

23
00:01:28.075 --> 00:01:33.333
Use a custom authentication strength
that names issuers or policy OIDs,

24
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.400
up to five of each, for
sensitive resources.

25
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.462
Require CRL validation; the program
wants each trusted issuing CA to

26
00:01:41.462 --> 00:01:46.613
publish a CRL at least every twenty-four
hours, because Entra caches it.

27
00:01:46.613 --> 00:01:51.071
And CA scoping, generally
available since April 2026,

28
00:01:51.071 --> 00:01:55.024
ties each CA to one group,
with up to thirty rules.

29
00:01:55.024 --> 00:01:57.980
A mistake can lock users out, so pilot it.
